SUMMARY:Economic Theory – Massimo Motta & IO workshop (Pompeu Fabra) – 
 Platform Tying and its Effects
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3059
DESCRIPTION:Massimo Motta & IO workshop: “Platform Tying and its Effects
 ”\nhttps://sites.google.com/site/massimomottawebpage/\n\nGoogle Maps: ht
 tps://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nWe study on-platform
  tying by a dominant platform that controls a primary access point and ope
 rates an adjacent specialised service. A rival service can reach users bot
 h through the dominant platform and through a direct channel. In a two-sid
 ed market where platforms charge sellers\, tying improves the integrated s
 ervice\, but also shifts demand away from the rival. This reduces seller p
 articipation on the rival platform\, weakening the rival also for users wh
 o access it directly. As a result\, tying can reduce consumer surplus and 
 welfare. We also compare tying with demotion and with a common-access poli
 cy\, and show that our main insights carry over to a one-sided model in wh
 ich network effects operate among consumers who pay directly for the speci
 alised service.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4735c8e83906adcaf6db38c516917508@generated
