SUMMARY:Economic Theory – Jiemai Wu (USydney) – Group cascades in strat
 egic voting
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3060
DESCRIPTION:Jiemai Wu: “Group cascades in strategic voting”\nhttps://ww
 w.jiemaiwu.com/\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\
 n\nABSTRACT:\nWe study observational learning in a sequential game with st
 rategic voting groups whose members have common values and receive indepen
 dent private signals. Each group votes strategically after observing all e
 arlier groups' decisions. Our model bridges the literatures on information
  cascades and strategic voting by replacing the individual decision makers
  in Bikhchandani et al. (1992) with the strategic voting groups in Fedders
 en and Pesendorfer (1998). We show that this game is not outcome-equivalen
 t to any standard individual cascade game if and only if the voting rule i
 s fixed across groups. We then identify the necessary condition under whic
 h a fixed rule that maximises asymptotic expected utility differs from one
  that maximises myopic expected utility. This difference is common and man
 ifests differently under private versus public voting: under private votin
 g\, relatively asymmetric rules - such as unanimity - are more advantageou
 s in the limit\, whereas the opposite can hold under public voting.
END:VEVENT
